        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "2e9d7ca4-ed09-510c-997a-fa51800282dc",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Places: Windermere, Cumbria; Bowness-on-Windermere; Cumbria, England; Kendal\n- Buildings: Windermere Hotel; Windermere railway station\n- People: Chad Stuart; Jeremy Clyde\n- Music Groups: Chad & Jeremy\n- Topics: railway development; town naming\n\nFacts:\n- In 1847, the railway link with Kendal was established, and Windermere railway station was named \"Windermere.\"\n- In 1847, the town of Windermere took its name from Lake Windermere when the railway line was built.\n- In 1847, Windermere Hotel opened near Windermere railway station in Windermere, Cumbria, England.\n- Windermere Hotel was originally called The Riggs Windermere.\n- The town of Windermere does not directly touch Lake Windermere.\n- Windermere has grown together with the older lakeside town of Bowness-on-Windermere, although both towns still have distinct centres.\n- Chad Stuart was born as David Stuart Chadwick on 10 December 1941 in Windermere, Cumbria.\n- Jeremy Clyde was born as Michael Thomas Jeremy Clyde on 22 March 1941 in Dorney, Buckinghamshire.\n- Chad & Jeremy are an English folk rock duo from the 1960s made up of Chad Stuart and Jeremy Clyde.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "d021e860-afce-548f-9b72-d057166a85b8",
        "text": "Page: Windermere Hotel (Lake District). Sentence: Windermere Hotel , originally The Riggs Windermere, is a hotel in Windermere, Cumbria, England, located near Windermere railway station.\nPage: Windermere Hotel (Lake District). Sentence: The hotel opened at the time that the railway link with Kendal was established in 1847.\nPage: Windermere, Cumbria (town). Sentence: Although the town Windermere does not touch the lake (it took the name of the lake when the railway line was built in 1847 and the station was called \"Windermere\"), it has now grown together with the older lakeside town of Bowness-on-Windermere, though the two retain distinguishable town centres.\nPage: Chad &amp; Jeremy. Sentence: Chad and Jeremy are an English singing folk rock duo originating in the 1960s, comprising Chad Stuart (born David Stuart Chadwick, 10 December 1941, Windermere, Cumbria) and Jeremy Clyde (born Michael Thomas Jeremy Clyde, 22 March 1941, Dorney, Buckinghamshire).",
